{title: As I Have Done}
{subtitle: John 13:1–17}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm7] | [Abmaj7] |
| [Bbsus4] [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]On the [Eb]night before the Passover, the [Cm7]supper on the board
The [Abmaj7]one who came from God and was [Bbsus4]going back to God
[Bb]Rose [Eb]up from the table and he laid his [Cm7]robe aside
Took a towel and a ba[Abmaj7]sin and he tied the cloth around
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He [Bbsus4]knelt before the fisher[Eb]men with dust upon their feet
He [Cm7]washed them one by one and [Abmaj7]dried them with the towel he wore
He [Bbsus4]came to Simon Pe[Bb]ter, who [Eb]pulled his feet away
You [Cm7]shall never wash my feet
[Abmaj7]Unless I wash you, you have [Bbsus4]no [Bb]share [Ab]with me
Lord, then not [Eb/G]only my feet, but my [Fm7]hands and my head as well
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I have [Bbsus4]given you an exam[Bb]ple
So that [Eb]you also should do as [Gm7]I have done for you
You [Ab]also ought to [Bbsus4]wash one another's [Bb][Eb]feet
As I have done for [Gm7]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]Hav[Bb]ing loved his own [Eb]who were in the [Cm7]world
He loved them to the very [Gm7]end
You call me [Ab]Teacher and Lord, and you are [Bb]right
No ser[Cm7]vant is greater than his mas[Gm7]ter
If you [Ab]know these things, you are blessed when you [Bb]do them
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I have [Ab]given you an ex[Eb/G]ample
So that you also [Eb]should do as I have done [Gm7]for you
You also ought [Ab]to wash one [Bb]another's feet
[Eb]As I have done for [Gm7]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Ab]He [Bb]loved them to the [Eb]very end [Cm7][Abmaj7]
As [Eb/G]I have done for [Bbsus4]you
{end_of_verse}

